{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And when He sent — and Elohim did not lead them by the way of the land of the Philistines.</b> Even though the divine intent was to bring Israel to Mount Sinai to receive the Torah, and from there to the land of Israel, as it says (Exodus 6:7–8): וְלָקַחְתִּי אֶתְכֶם לִי לְעָם וְהֵבֵאתִי אֶתְכֶם אֶל הָאָרֶץ — nevertheless the intent now was to lead them to the Sea of Reeds, which was on the way to neither of these, in order to drown Pharaoh and his army there, after the manner of (Judges 4:7): וּמָשַׁכְתִּי אֵלֶיךָ אֶל נַחַל קִישׁוֹן אֶת סִיסְרָא. Now the straight and short way to go from Egypt to the Sea of Reeds was the way of the land of the Philistines; he says that the blessed El did not wish to lead them by that route." "<b>Because it is near.</b> Because that route and its terminus were close to Egypt, and travelers pass there frequently and report from there to Egypt and from Egypt to there." "And so <b>when they see war.</b> When they hear that Pharaoh is preparing himself to pursue them with all his army, the people will assuredly lose heart from fear of their warfare and return to Egypt. Therefore He turned them onto a road on which no person had traveled."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:24.370622458Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}